On Mon, 9 Aug 2004, Robin Lee Powell wrote:

> On Sun, Aug 08, 2004 at 06:34:18AM -0400, Pierre Abbat wrote:
> > http://jbo.wikipedia.org
> >
> What's the point?

Using Lojban for something wortwhile, I suppose.

> Everyone here speaks another language; why bother to repeat the same
> information?

The information contained therein need not be repetitions of the
information contained within other wikipedias. Wouldn't it be nice for a
change if there was some information available in Lojban that was not
available in other languages?

> More relevantly, I'm leary of Yet Another Project starting up when I
> can't even get but two or three people to help with the BPFK on a
> serious basis.

I wouldn't refer to it as Yet Another Project. Most Wikipedia contributors
are casual about their edits, and prefer to add or fix small things at
their leisure. Contributing to Wikipedia does not entail any commitment to
getting it done. While there is some interlanguage competition on WP,
languages with few articles or little activity is not frequently a subject
of ridicule.

Also, why are you mentioning BPFK? Participating in an activity related to
Lojban does not detract from the time available to other Lojban
activities. At least not for me.

